From 4482f55bec02432dd0be5cc205efc20c30c14d00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin Inglis <giinglis@amazon.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:40:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ztoc: link zlib statically without the -l:libz.a cgo flag

Go 1.26.11 and 1.27.4 tightened the cgo linker flag allowlist in
cmd/go/internal/work/security.go, so the ztoc/compression package
fails to build:

  invalid flag in #cgo LDFLAGS: -l:libz.a (see https://go.dev/s/invalidflag)

Use `-Wl,--push-state,-Bstatic -lz -Wl,--pop-state` instead. All three
flags are on the allowlist, and the result is the same: the linker
searches the -L directories and the system library path for libz.a
only, so zlib is still linked statically.

Signed-off-by: Gavin Inglis <giinglis@amazon.com>
---
 ztoc/compression/gzip_zinfo.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ztoc/compression/gzip_zinfo.go b/ztoc/compression/gzip_zinfo.go
index 697de80..51644cc 100644
--- a/ztoc/compression/gzip_zinfo.go
+++ b/ztoc/compression/gzip_zinfo.go
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 package compression

 // #cgo CFLAGS: -I${SRCDIR}/
-// #cgo LDFLAGS: -L${SRCDIR}/../out -l:libz.a
+// #cgo LDFLAGS: -L${SRCDIR}/../out -Wl,--push-state,-Bstatic -lz -Wl,--pop-state
 // #include "gzip_zinfo.h"
 // #include <stdlib.h>
 // #include <stdint.h>
--
2.50.1

